WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.900
Recorded at the department of Dr. Muir at the College for Tropical Medicine

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.400
and the Alberth Victoria Hospital in Calcutta.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:12.120
The outpatient material is examined at the research facility, sorted by stages and forms

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:17.140
and the patients are either treated as outpatients or admitted to one of the leprosy hospitals.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:20.100
Here follows first the initial stages.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:25.860
Nerve case (category A1). The anesthetic area is outlined with a skin marker.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:42.800
Nerve case (category A2). Displays the leprous thickening of the nerves, plaques and early nodules.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:47.460
Moving on to skin affections.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:12.060
Nerve-skin case (category A2-B1). Numerous lesions in the face, upper body and

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:15.120
the extremities.

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:21.660
The thickened nerve is indicated by a finger. Occasionally, in the middle of the nodules,

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:27.300
you will observe visibly dark areas which result from the excising of specimens. One sees that large areas of the skin are

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:32.940
depigmented with plaques and growing early nodules. The cases described so far,

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:38.280
were preliminarily described as negative. The exact diagnosis could only be established

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:47.820
based on sensitivity tests and bacteriological examination of nasal secretion

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:52.400
and small excised skin samples.

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:35.440
The following case clearly shows the process of infection. A barber working at the bazaar in

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:41.920
the countryside typically shaves the healthy and the infected indiscriminately, and in this way is infected with leprosy.

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:48.160
You can observe how a heavily infected leprosy patient (category B3-B2) is shaved by the barber.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:55.580
In the place on the forearm where he rubs off the soap, the barber has developed an anesthetic plaque (category A1).

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:38.870
Skin case (category B1).

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:48.900
Skin case (category B2).
Ear and knee affected.

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:11.640
Skin case (category B2).
Both earlobes affected.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:25.820
Skin case (category B2). The nasal secretion showed a strong positive reaction--the skin lesions were also positive.

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:43.720
Skin case (category B2). Only the smear tests were positive, not the epithelial tissue.

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:56.940
The Albert-Victoria Hospital. The facilities.

00:04:56.940 --> 00:05:03.620
The patients move about completely freely, so far as their health allows,

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:07.060
and keep themselves busy.

00:05:55.740 --> 00:06:00.960
Severe skin case (category B3-B2-A2). The most severe changes are found in the face and the upper extremities.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:05.980
The anesthetic lesions are expressions of category A2.

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:34.540
Nerve case (category A1-A2). Characterized by anesthesia--in the shape of a glove--and tropical disorders of

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:39.900
the skin, along with nodules artificially created by the treatment.

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:28.460
This is a skin case (category B3) that has improved to category B2-A2. The treatment has shrunk the

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:36.280
previously inflamed skin and has produced the so-called "shrunken elephant skin."

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:18.980
Skin case (category B3-A2). Leonine facies (lion face) with severe tropical damage in the

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:21.940
extremities. Toes have been lost.

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:55.180
Both the following two cases (category B3 to A2) show swellings and tuberous changes in the

00:08:55.180 --> 00:09:00.160
skin that is of particular interest. The first shows ulcers in the eyelids, while

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:05.140
the second has expressed nodular changes in the eyeball.

00:09:28.780 --> 00:09:35.420
The following two cases show a variety of skin and nerve conditions (category B3-A2), with profound tropical

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:43.240
ulcers, tropical skin changes, mutilations, clawed hand, Facies Leonidas (lion face) and tuberous lesions.

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:20.120
The treatment of leprosy with chaulmoogra oil obtained from trees planted in the hospital garden itself.

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:26.720
The oil is recovered from Hydnocarpus Whightiana, and the treatment is administered as a combination of injections and

00:10:26.720 --> 00:10:32.800
inunctions of the patients. The injections take place using a specially designed short and thick

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:38.060
injection needle intracutaneously. Both the oil and esters of the fruit are used.

00:10:38.060 --> 00:10:43.420
The intracutaneous injections are administered once or twice a week, in doses of one to five cubic centimeters, which is injected

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:49.480
under the skin to create nodules measuring between a half and three quarters of a cubic centimeter. The dosage must be carefully

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:55.880
made, and controlled by determining the sedimentation rate of the blood, in order to avoid severe

00:10:55.880 --> 00:11:00.120
local and general reactions.

